A 2-in-1 touchscreen sends clicks to the wrong location, but a USB mouse works fine. What should you try FIRST?	Recalibrate the touchscreen	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A 3-year-old iPad's battery life dropped from 8+ hours to 30-60 minutes. What action should be taken?	Replace the battery	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A 6-month-old Android phone became slow after installing a new stock market tracking app. What action should you take?	Uninstall the newly installed app to confirm it's the cause of the slowdown	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A BYOD policy needs to secure corporate apps/data on personal phones while respecting employee privacy. Which solution best balances this?	MDM with containerization — a separate managed corporate profile/container, leaving personal data and apps untouched	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A Google Pixel with a third-party keyboard app becomes slow, and the keyboard stops responding after 6 months. What is the FIRST solution to try?	Uninstall (or reinstall) the third-party virtual keyboard app	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A Windows 10 laptop's touch screen isn't working properly. What should you check FIRST?	Whether the touchscreen is enabled/recognized in Device Manager and its driver is installed correctly	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A car GPS says you're driving south, but the car's compass shows north. What should be done?	Recalibrate the compass — it's being affected by magnetic interference (from the vehicle's metal/electronics)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A company tablet lost access to corporate email/files because its OS is outdated (updates were skipped). How would you resolve this?	Update the device's OS to the version required by corporate compliance/MDM policy	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A customer's smartphone feels warm and the battery appears swollen/bulging. What is the BEST advice?	Stop using and charging it immediately (power it off) and have the battery professionally replaced — a swollen battery is a fire/safety hazard	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A dropped touchscreen laptop has spiderweb cracks but still displays images correctly and responds to touch. Which component needs replacement?	The outer glass/digitizer panel	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A friend's iPhone runs iOS 15 and was purchased in 2020. What charging cable do they need?	A Lightning cable	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A gaming laptop has only 1 USB port but needs a mouse, keyboard, and webcam connected, with a $20 budget. What should be purchased?	A USB hub	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A hotspot's upload speed drops from 25 Mbps to 0.125 Mbps after 20-30 minutes of continuous use. What is MOST likely the cause?	The carrier is throttling the connection after exceeding a data/tethering usage threshold	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop connected to school Wi-Fi yesterday but won't connect today, while everyone else's laptops connect fine. What should you check FIRST?	Whether Wi-Fi is toggled on (and airplane mode is off) on the laptop	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop connects to an iPhone over Wi-Fi to use its cellular data connection. What is this called?	Tethering (Wi-Fi hotspot)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop connects to an iPhone via USB cable to use its cellular data. What is this configuration called?	USB tethering	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop displays "Theqickbrwnfxjmpedverthelazydg" instead of "The quick brown fox..." — the O, U, and space bar aren't registering. What is MOST likely the issue?	Those specific keys are dirty, stuck, or physically damaged (debris under the O, U, and space bar) — clean or replace the keyboard	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop keyboard has several non-responsive keys. What is the most appropriate FIRST step?	Clean the keyboard (compressed air) to remove debris before considering replacement	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop reportedly had a glass of water spilled on it. What are the FIRST steps in troubleshooting it?	Power it off immediately, remove the battery, and let it fully dry before attempting to power it back on	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop that was recently dropped can't detect any wireless networks, though the Wi-Fi card shows current drivers in Device Manager. What should you do next?	Check the internal wireless antenna cable connections — the drop likely disconnected/damaged them	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop trackpad is unresponsive after waking from sleep but works fine with a USB mouse. What should you check first?	The touchpad's power management/driver settings (USB selective suspend can disable it on wake)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop trackpad lost multi-touch gesture support after an OS update, though basic cursor movement still works, and a restart didn't help. What should you do next?	Update or reinstall the trackpad driver	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A laptop webcam produces a blurry image; drivers are current and it's properly detected. What is the most likely cause?	The camera lens is physically dirty/smudged and needs cleaning	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A mobile device can't connect to corporate Wi-Fi after switching from a home network. What should you check first?	The correct security/authentication type (certificate, EAP method, SSID/password) required by the corporate network	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A mobile device isn't charging over a USB-A to USB-C cable and isn't detected by the computer. What is the FIRST diagnostic step?	Try a different known-good cable and/or port to isolate whether the cable, port, or device is at fault	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A mobile device using a traditional HDD has become significantly slower over time. What is the MOST effective upgrade?	Replace the HDD with an SSD	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A mobile device's battery drains unusually fast even after a full charge. What should you do FIRST?	Check the battery usage statistics to identify which app/process is draining the battery	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A phone can't connect to home Wi-Fi but other devices connect fine. What should the technician check NEXT?	Forget/remove the saved Wi-Fi network on the phone and reconnect (check for a stale profile or MAC filtering on the router)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A phone gets 8761 kbps on cellular, but a laptop tethered to its hotspot only gets 243 kbps. What is MOST likely the cause?	The phone's Wi-Fi hotspot radio/2.4 GHz band is the bottleneck (interference or hotspot throughput limits), not the cellular connection	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A phone's screen flickers and the battery won't charge consistently. What should you ask the user FIRST?	Whether the phone was recently dropped or exposed to liquid/damage	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A smartphone left in a hot car won't turn on when retrieved. What MOST likely happened?	The device/battery overheated and shut down for thermal protection — let it cool before powering on	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A smartphone shows a question mark next to the Wi-Fi icon after connecting to "FreeAirportWiFi" — calls work, but websites don't load. What is MOST likely the issue?	The public Wi-Fi requires captive portal authentication (open a browser to sign in before internet access is granted)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A smartphone's hotspot speed drops from 24 Mbps to 256 Kbps. What is MOST likely the problem?	The carrier is throttling tethered/hotspot data usage	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A smartphone's touchscreen isn't responding to touch. What is the FIRST step to try?	Restart (reboot) the device	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A stolen company smartphone is still communicating with the MDM system. What should the technician do next to protect data confidentiality?	Issue a remote wipe of the device through the MDM	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A touchscreen laptop is non-responsive to touch, though the touchpad works fine and the screen looks undamaged. Which component needs replacement?	The digitizer	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A user can't complete NFC payments after an OS update, though the store's terminal works for other customers. What is the most logical first step?	Check that NFC is still enabled in the phone's settings (the update may have disabled it)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
A user needs their phone to last all day at a conference with scarce outlets while staying available for updates. What should they use?	A portable battery pack/power bank (and enable battery saver mode)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
After installing a replacement wireless card in a laptop with "Main" and "Aux" antenna cables, what is the most important step before reassembly?	Connect each antenna cable to its correct matching connector on the card (Main to Main, Aux to Aux)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
After removing the old webcam module during a laptop webcam replacement, what should the technician do next before installing the new one?	Follow proper ESD precautions and inspect the connector/cable for damage before connecting the replacement module	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
After setting up a new iPhone, YouTube works but AirPods won't connect. What is MOST likely the problem?	Bluetooth is disabled, or the AirPods aren't paired correctly — enable Bluetooth and pair the AirPods	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An Android phone's screen was replaced; it works fine in a dark room but is dim and hard to read with lights on. What is MOST likely the problem?	The ambient light sensor was damaged or disconnected during the screen replacement	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An MDM alert says a company phone is "not compliant" because it's missing a passcode. What should you do to resolve it?	Have the user set a passcode (or push the passcode policy via MDM) so the device becomes compliant and regains access	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An employee logs in with a username, password, and a one-time code texted to their phone. What is this authentication method called?	Multi-factor authentication (MFA) using SMS one-time passcode (OTP)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An employee syncs their Android phone's email with a corporate Office 365 account. What credentials will they need?	Their corporate Office 365 (Exchange) username/email address and password	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An employee's device uses excessive data because the email app downloads large attachments automatically. How would you optimize it?	Disable automatic attachment downloads (or configure the email app to only sync/download over Wi-Fi)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An executive traveling to Italy wants secure communications regardless of which Wi-Fi network she connects to. What should she set up before leaving?	A VPN subscription/client configured on her laptop before travel	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An iPad with 21% battery was left charging overnight and is now completely dead; the same Lightning cable also fails to charge an iPhone. What is MOST likely the reason?	The Lightning cable (or wall adapter) itself is faulty	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
An iPhone won't connect to a known Wi-Fi network, though the network works on other devices. What should be tried NEXT?	Forget the network on the iPhone and reconnect (re-enter credentials)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Bluetooth headphones are in pairing mode, but the smartphone doesn't detect them. What should you advise next?	Restart both devices, remove any old paired profile, and retry pairing within range (checking for interference)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Enabling airplane mode disables an employee's external mouse and headphones. What technology is being disabled?	Bluetooth	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
How can you test whether paired Bluetooth headphones are actually connected?	Play audio and confirm it comes through the headphones (or check that the device shows "Connected" in Bluetooth settings)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
How do you connect a smartphone to a car's built-in stereo to make/receive calls?	Pair the phone to the stereo via Bluetooth	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Traveling with unreliable cellular coverage and needing offline documents, what is the primary advantage of manual sync over automatic sync?	Manual sync lets you control exactly when syncing happens (e.g., only on a strong connection), avoiding failed/partial syncs and saving battery and data	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What connector type is most often used on older smartphones?	Micro-USB	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What converts the analog signal from tapping/swiping a touchscreen into a binary signal for the OS?	The digitizer	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What is the primary advantage of an eSIM compared to a traditional physical SIM card?	It requires no physical card and can be reprogrammed or switched between carriers remotely, without swapping hardware	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What is the primary advantage of biometric authentication compared to traditional passwords?	It's tied to a unique physical trait that's harder to steal, share, forget, or guess than a password	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What is the primary purpose of a data cap imposed by a mobile carrier?	To limit/control how much data a subscriber can use, managing network congestion and cost	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What must be enabled on a mobile device to allow internet access when cellular data is unavailable, such as in airplane mode?	Wi-Fi	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What must you do before tethering a phone to create a hotspot?	Enable the hotspot/tethering feature on the phone (and confirm the carrier plan allows it)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What precaution is most important when replacing an SSD in a mobile device?	Use proper ESD (anti-static) precautions — anti-static wrist strap/mat	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What single device lets you quickly connect an external monitor, keyboard, and mouse to a laptop through one connection?	A docking station (or USB-C hub)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
What type of cable connects the keyboard internally during a laptop keyboard replacement?	A ribbon cable (flexible printed circuit/FPC)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Where are the antenna wires typically located within a laptop or mobile device?	Routed around/behind the display bezel, near the top of the LCD screen	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which MDM feature ensures only approved corporate apps can be installed on a managed device?	Application allowlisting (a managed/approved app catalog)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which MDM feature should be enabled to protect data on a lost or stolen mobile device?	Remote wipe	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which USB connection type can supply up to 4.5 watts of power per device?	USB 3.0	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which USB connection type supports data rates up to 480 Mbps?	USB 2.0 (Hi-Speed USB)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which USB connector is reversible and commonly found on most modern mobile devices?	USB-C	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which accessory would be MOST useful for a mobile professional needing hands-free communication?	A Bluetooth headset	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which biometric technology analyzes physical traits visible from a distance, avoiding close-up interaction?	Facial recognition	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cable is NOT used by Android smartphones and tablets?	The Lightning cable (Apple-proprietary, used only on Apple devices)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cable type supports both charging and data transfer with a reversible (non-directional) connector?	USB-C	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cellular technology combines HSPA+ and EV-DO for higher data speeds than earlier protocols?	3G	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cellular technology comprises LTE and LTE-A for higher data speeds than earlier protocols?	4G	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cellular technology uses a SIM card to identify the subscriber on a provider's network?	GSM	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which cellular technology uses new frequency bands to reach proposed speeds of at least 20 Gbps?	5G	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which connection type allows short-range wireless communication commonly used for data transfer and payment processing?	NFC (Near Field Communication)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which connectivity option provides the fastest wired data transfer speeds for mobile devices?	USB-C (USB 3.1/3.2 or Thunderbolt)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which device should help desk agents use to provide voice-only VoIP support without video?	A headset (with microphone)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which feature lets you share your smartphone's cellular internet connection with multiple devices simultaneously?	Mobile hotspot (Wi-Fi tethering)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which mobile accessory is a small, pressure-sensitive nub used as a pointing device on laptops?	A pointing stick (TrackPoint-style nub)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which mobile sync feature reduces data usage for devices with limited data plans?	Syncing only over Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi-only/selective sync), rather than over cellular data	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which of the following is NOT considered part of the Internet of Things (IoT)?	A standard, non-networked device (e.g., a traditional desktop PC) — IoT refers to embedded/smart connected devices like thermostats, cameras, and appliances	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which setting can slow down the trackpad cursor speed in Windows 10?	Adjust pointer/cursor speed in the Mouse or Touchpad settings	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology BEST generates a simple square code easily scanned by a smartphone to open a preconfigured link?	A QR code	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology inventories equipment using a chip-programmed tag with one-way communication to a reader?	RFID (passive RFID tags)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology manages personal laptops/smartphones under a telework/BYOD policy, providing security updates and remote administration?	MDM (Mobile Device Management)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology provides precise latitude/longitude using a constellation of 24 satellites?	GPS	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology provides the precise latitude and longitude of a device's location outdoors?	GPS	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology reads employee ID badges with embedded electronic chips to log into computers?	An RFID (or smart card) reader	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which technology should be used to install a custom corporate app (not in the public App Store) and its security profile onto employees' iPhones?	MDM (with enterprise/in-house app deployment, e.g., via Apple Business Manager)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which two things does a CDMA smartphone use to connect to the cellular network while traveling? (Select TWO)	ESN (Electronic Serial Number) and MIN/MEID (Mobile Identification/Equipment Number)	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
Which wearable BEST lets a busy business owner quickly view email/IM notifications and stay in contact while moving between meetings?	A smartwatch	CompTIA_A+::Mobile_Devices
20 computers on a single 24-port hub are causing excessive collisions. Which device should be installed to reduce them?	A switch (replacing the hub)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
33 computers connect to two switches via CAT5e, with the switches interconnected by fiber (MTRJ) — all within one building. What type of network is this?	A LAN (using a fiber backbone/interconnect within a single building)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A Zigbee-based hub controls lights, HVAC, and power in a studio. What type of networked host is this?	An IoT (Internet of Things) hub/smart-home device	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A buried copper cable link between two buildings fails during nearby construction, with a non-temporary outage. What is the MOST likely cause?	The underground cable was physically cut/damaged by the construction work	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A business orders a microwave service for 1 Gbps connectivity with under 10 ms latency outside standard service areas. What type of internet connection is this?	Fixed wireless (licensed microwave) internet	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A company replaced all switches with Layer 3 multilayer switches so VoIP devices could be placed on separate VLANs with routed packets. What segmentation technique is this?	VLAN segmentation with inter-VLAN routing (Layer 3 switching)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A customer's ipconfig shows an IP address of 169.254.12.45. What is the root cause of their internet issue?	The device couldn't reach a DHCP server and self-assigned an APIPA address	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A cybersecurity analyst needs to capture a copy of all traffic between a router and firewall without being in-line. Which tool is required?	A network tap (or a switch's SPAN/mirror port)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A duplicate IP address error persists across reboots when logging into a workstation. What is MOST likely the cause?	A statically-assigned IP address is conflicting with another device on the network	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A laptop connects to wireless, can ping the gateway and 8.8.8.8, but can't reach google.com. What should you check NEXT?	The DNS server configuration	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A laptop connects with CAT5e but gets IP 169.254.13.52 and can't reach a website. What is MOST likely the cause?	The DHCP server is unreachable, so the laptop assigned itself an APIPA address	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A network printer plugged into a switch shows a green link light but can't obtain an IP address automatically. What is a potential reason?	The DHCP server's address scope is exhausted (no available leases), or the printer's NIC is misconfigured (e.g., set to static)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A new Smart TV can't reach Netflix and shows IP address 169.254.0.24. What type of address is this?	An APIPA (link-local) address — the DHCP server is unreachable	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A new laptop displays "IP address conflict with another system." What should you do?	Release and renew the IP address (or assign a unique static IP) to resolve the duplicate address	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A newly installed WAP is sporadically dropping connections. What should be checked FIRST?	Wireless interference/channel overlap with nearby access points (and AP placement)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A point-to-multipoint microwave radio link through a wooded area pings fine but users report sporadic connectivity. What is the MOST likely cause?	Trees/foliage are attenuating or obstructing the line-of-sight signal (worsened by wind, rain, or leaf growth)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A switch's physical interfaces are continually going up and down (port flapping) for two workstations. What is the MOST likely cause?	A faulty cable or connector (or a duplex/speed mismatch)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A user calls saying their laptop can't connect to the corporate wireless network. What should the technician do FIRST per troubleshooting methodology?	Identify the problem — gather information from the user	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A user has slow Wi-Fi speeds only in their large apartment building, though the device works fine elsewhere. What should they do?	Change the Wi-Fi channel to reduce interference/congestion from neighboring networks (or move to the 5 GHz band)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A workstation can access http://www.diontraining.com but not the https version. Which port should be unblocked?	Port 80 (HTTP)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A workstation can ping 8.8.8.8 but cannot reach Facebook.com by name. What server is likely at fault?	The DNS server	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A workstation can't access https://www.diontraining.com but can access the http version. Which port should be unblocked?	Port 443 (HTTPS)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A workstation can't reach diontraining.com by name but can by IP. Which port should be unblocked?	Port 53 (DNS)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
A workstation randomly loses network connectivity multiple times a day. After gathering info, what troubleshooting step comes NEXT?	Establish a theory of probable cause	CompTIA_A+::Networking
After a Windows 10 security update, network speeds dropped from 1 Gbps to 100 Mbps on all workstations. What is MOST likely the cause?	The update reverted/corrupted the NIC driver or introduced a speed/duplex mismatch	CompTIA_A+::Networking
After creating user accounts on a new Windows server, what must be configured next to give users access to data on the server's partition?	Share and NTFS (file/folder) permissions	CompTIA_A+::Networking
After implementing a solution for a network problem, what is the NEXT step in the CompTIA troubleshooting methodology?	Verify full system functionality (and implement preventive measures if applicable)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
After replacing an access point with an 802.11ac model, a 7-year-old wireless printer won't connect. What is MOST likely the reason?	The old printer only supports an older standard/security type (e.g., 802.11g/n or WEP/WPA) that isn't compatible with the new AP's configuration	CompTIA_A+::Networking
An 802.11b card can't see an 802.11g router's SSID (Dion-Corp) when scanning in Windows. What is the MOST likely reason?	The SSID broadcast is disabled (a hidden network), so it won't appear in a normal scan	CompTIA_A+::Networking
An FTP connection to a remote server keeps failing to open. What should you do FIRST to resolve it?	Verify the firewall isn't blocking FTP (port 21), and confirm the FTP server is reachable/online	CompTIA_A+::Networking
An existing wireless network only offers three non-overlapping channels, but more are needed to avoid interference with neighboring businesses. Which standard should be implemented?	A standard supporting the 5 GHz band (e.g., 802.11n/ac/ax), which offers many more non-overlapping channels than 2.4 GHz	CompTIA_A+::Networking
An iPhone connects to a car stereo over Bluetooth to play podcasts. What type of network is this?	A PAN (Personal Area Network)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
At a punchdown block, one wire in a wall-jack circuit appears loose. How should the technician fix it with the punchdown tool?	Re-seat the wire firmly into its correct slot with the punchdown tool, trimming any excess wire	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Cat5e cable is being run near fluorescent lights in a drop ceiling with no cable trays. What type of CAT5e cable should be run?	Shielded (STP) CAT5e cable, to reduce EMI from the fluorescent lights	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Connecting several campus area networks together across a city forms what type of network?	A MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Dion Training created an A record for DionTraining.com, but www.DionTraining.com gives an error. What DNS record fixes this?	A CNAME record aliasing www to the root domain	CompTIA_A+::Networking
During VoIP calls, a caller's voice speeds up and slows down even though they speak at a constant rate. Which metric explains this?	Jitter	CompTIA_A+::Networking
During passive DNS reconnaissance, which record identifies the authoritative DNS server for a domain?	The NS (Name Server) record (and the SOA record)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Employees are only allowed to receive email on one device, and mail should be removed from the server once downloaded. Which mail protocol should be configured?	POP3	CompTIA_A+::Networking
How does a DHCP reservation work?	It assigns a specific IP address to a device (matched by its MAC address) from the DHCP pool, so that device always receives the same IP	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Installing an 802.11ax access point inside an office creates what type of network?	A WLAN (Wireless Local Area Network)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Most users get up to 300 Mbps on an 802.11n network, but a few with 802.11n cards are capped at 108 Mbps. What should the technician do?	Update the affected NICs' drivers/firmware so they support channel bonding (40 MHz channels) like the rest of the network	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Neighboring offices use 2.4 GHz B/G/N routers; you install your own 2.4 GHz AP (security system uses 5 GHz) and want to maximize channel separation. Which channels should you configure?	Channels 1 and 11 (the widest-spaced non-overlapping channels)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
On which device would you configure an ACL (access control list) to implement a network security policy?	A router (or firewall/Layer 3 switch)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
STP cable pairs are not completely twisted near the connector. What issue may result?	Increased crosstalk/EMI interference on the cable	CompTIA_A+::Networking
The accounting department is relocated over 70 meters from the closest IDF, and an SLA requires 10 Gb speeds. What media should be installed?	Fiber optic cable (or CAT6a, which supports 10GBASE-T up to 100 meters)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Three 802.11a devices can't associate with an 802.11g access point configured with WEP, despite being within 20 feet. What is MOST likely the cause?	802.11a and 802.11g use incompatible frequency bands (802.11a is 5 GHz-only; the AP is 2.4 GHz-only 802.11g), so they can't associate	CompTIA_A+::Networking
To block a ransomware exploit targeting the Windows SMB protocol, which port should be added to the firewall blocklist?	Port 445	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Two of three 802.11g APs use Channel 1 and Channel 11. Which channel should the third AP use to avoid overlap?	Channel 6	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Two of three 802.11g APs use Channel 11 and Channel 6. Which channel should the third AP use to avoid overlap?	Channel 1	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Users at an adjacent building lose connectivity intermittently after a new flagpole was installed; SSID/encryption/channels on the 802.11ac bridge are all confirmed correct. What is MOST likely the cause?	The flagpole is physically obstructing the line-of-sight/Fresnel zone of the wireless bridge link	CompTIA_A+::Networking
Users report duplicate IP address errors and can't reach the file server or browse websites. Which server should be checked FIRST?	The DHCP server	CompTIA_A+::Networking
VoIP calls keep dropping on a network with a single 48-port gigabit Layer 3 switch serving desktops, laptops, and VoIP devices. What should be done to prevent dropped calls?	Segment VoIP devices onto a separate VLAN with QoS prioritization	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What describes the IP address of the router that packets destined for a remote network are sent to by default?	The default gateway	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What does the IPv6 address ::1 represent?	The loopback address (equivalent to IPv4's 127.0.0.1)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What internet offer would provide Jason the FASTEST service from a fiber provider?	The offer with the highest available symmetrical bandwidth (Gbps fiber plan)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What is an advantage of 2.4 GHz devices over 5.0 GHz devices?	Longer range and better penetration through walls/obstacles	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What is an advantage of the 6 GHz Wi-Fi band over 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz?	More available spectrum/non-overlapping channels, resulting in less congestion and interference (Wi-Fi 6E)	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What is the MOST likely reason for replacing all network hubs with switches?	Switches give each port its own collision domain, eliminating the collisions/shared bandwidth inherent to hubs	CompTIA_A+::Networking
What is the main difference between a punchdown tool and a crimping tool?	A punchdown tool terminates wires into fixed connectors like punch-down blocks/keystone jacks, while a crimping tool attaches connectors (like RJ45 plugs) onto the end of a cable	CompTIA_A+::Networking
