Which storage device form factor is NOT used in laptops?	3.5-inch desktop drive form factor	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which storage type uses a NAND chipset mounted directly on the motherboard instead of a mechanical spinning drive?	eMMC storage (or an M.2 NVMe SSD)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which tool removes the jacket/sheathing from a wire when building a cable?	A wire stripper (cable stripper)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of RAM module should be selected to add 8 GB of RAM to a laptop?	A SODIMM	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of hard disk drive would be installed in a low-end office desktop?	A standard 5400/7200 RPM SATA HDD (economical, lower-performance)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of hard disk drive would provide the best performance in a gaming workstation?	A high-RPM (10,000-15,000 RPM) HDD, or ideally an SSD	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of laptop display uses a fluorescent backlight to illuminate the image?	A CCFL-backlit LCD display	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of memory allows a server to keep working even if data corruption occurs within a memory module?	ECC (Error-Correcting Code) RAM	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which type of power supply lets the installer attach/remove cables as needed to reduce clutter?	A modular power supply	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which version of USB can operate at speeds up to 5 Gbps?	USB 3.0 (USB 3.1 Gen 1)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
Which virtualization technology is supported by most modern Intel processors?	Intel VT-x	CompTIA_A+::Hardware
"Shadow PC" is a virtualized Windows gaming PC accessed from anywhere in the cloud. What type of service is this?	DaaS (Desktop as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A CRM app is offered to multiple businesses as a subscription, each with separate data but shared infrastructure. Which cloud model best fits?	SaaS (multi-tenant Software as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A VM running an older legacy OS works, but the software freezes/runs slowly. What is the likely cause, and the fix?	The VM isn't allocated enough resources (CPU/RAM) — increase the VM's allocated resources	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A VM running in sandbox mode crashed after a software patch installation. What should the technician do next?	Revert the VM to a snapshot taken before the patch was applied	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A VM with dynamic disk allocation frequently runs out of storage during testing. What is the likely cause, and the fix?	Dynamically allocated disks grow as needed and can exhaust host storage — free up/add host storage, or resize/compact the virtual disk	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A cloud app uses excessive CPU even during low traffic, raising costs. How can elasticity fix this?	Configure auto-scaling so resources automatically scale down/deallocate when demand is low	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A cloud backup bill shows an unexpected spike due to "egress traffic." What does this refer to?	Data transferred out of (downloaded from) the cloud provider's network — outbound traffic that providers typically charge for	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A cloud service automatically adds resources during a traffic spike. What cloud characteristic is this?	Elasticity (rapid elasticity/on-demand scalability)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A company purchases cloud storage dedicated solely to its own use due to privacy concerns. Which cloud type is this?	Private cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A company uses both on-premise storage and cloud-based storage together. What type of cloud is this?	Hybrid cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A company wants cloud accounting to cut costs, but some worry about sharing financial data with other companies. What solution addresses both concerns?	A private (or community) cloud, dedicated to the organization rather than shared multi-tenant infrastructure	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A cross-platform virtualization environment fails to launch after a platform update. What should the technician do FIRST?	Check for compatibility issues with the update (verify virtualization is still enabled in BIOS/UEFI, and consider rolling back or reinstalling the virtualization platform)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A cybersecurity analyst uses a sandboxed VM to analyze a file that attempts unauthorized system changes and network access. Why is the sandbox critical here?	It isolates and contains the malicious file, preventing it from affecting the host system or the real network during analysis	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A developer wants to test an app on multiple OSes without buying separate computers, running on top of their existing Windows desktop. Which virtualization technology should they use?	A Type 2 (hosted) hypervisor, such as VMware Workstation or VirtualBox	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
A small company purchases on-demand cloud storage from a commercial provider like Google Drive. What type of cloud is this?	Public cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
An IaaS database server has frequent downtime during peak hours due to heavy resource usage. What is the most effective solution?	Scale up/out the allocated resources (or enable auto-scaling/elasticity) for the server	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
An organization needs to run a Windows-based inventory app on Linux-based infrastructure. Which solution would BEST meet this requirement?	Run a Windows VM on a hypervisor hosted on the Linux infrastructure (or use an application compatibility layer)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
How can a company reduce software licensing costs while keeping remote access to its application server?	Implement Remote Desktop Services (terminal services)/thin clients so multiple users share one licensed application instance	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
How does application virtualization resolve running a legacy app incompatible with the current OS?	It streams/runs the app in an isolated virtual environment/container on the client, without installing it natively on the incompatible OS	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
How does cross-platform application virtualization let a legacy Windows app run on macOS?	It runs/streams the Windows app in an isolated virtualized environment on macOS, without requiring a full native Windows installation	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Microsoft 365 provides software accessed via a browser without local installation. What type of cloud service is this?	SaaS (Software as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Migrating an on-premise email server to a vendor-hosted web solution like Google Workspace/Gmail is an example of what cloud model?	SaaS (Software as a Service, delivered via public cloud)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Running multiple VMs on a Type II hypervisor, adding one more VM causes the host and all VMs to perform poorly with high CPU/memory usage. What should be done FIRST?	Review and reduce/reallocate the CPU and RAM assigned to the VMs (or add more host RAM) rather than adding more VMs	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Signing up for a cloud provider's programming environment to develop a mobile app is an example of which service type?	PaaS (Platform as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Using virtual machines to provision workstations for corporate users is an example of what technology?	VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What best explains the characteristics of a Type II hypervisor?	It installs and runs as an application on top of an existing host operating system	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What does VDI stand for?	Virtual Desktop Infrastructure	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is a key advantage of using containers for a web app that must run consistently across dev, test, and production?	Containers package the app with its dependencies, so it runs identically regardless of differences in the underlying environment	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is a key characteristic of a Type I hypervisor?	It runs directly on the physical hardware (bare-metal) without needing a host operating system	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is a key characteristic of a Type II hypervisor?	It runs as an application on top of a host operating system (instead of directly on hardware)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is a key feature of IaaS that makes it suitable for flexible traffic scaling?	IaaS offers on-demand, scalable compute/storage resources (rapid elasticity) without owning physical hardware	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is a primary benefit of using VDI?	Centralized management (patching, security, deployment) of desktops at the datacenter, rather than distributed across individual devices	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is the primary architectural difference between Type 1 and Type 2 hypervisors?	A Type 1 hypervisor runs directly on the physical hardware (bare-metal); a Type 2 hypervisor runs as an application on top of a host operating system	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is the primary benefit of using virtual network segmentation in a virtualization environment?	It isolates VM traffic into separate logical networks (improving security, reducing broadcast domains) without needing additional physical network hardware	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is the primary characteristic of multitenancy in a public cloud environment?	Multiple customers (tenants) share the same physical infrastructure while their data and resources remain logically isolated from each other	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What is the purpose of containers in virtualization?	They provide lightweight, OS-level virtualization that packages an app with its dependencies to run consistently, without a full separate guest OS	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What key cloud computing characteristic allows resources to be allocated/deallocated automatically as needed?	Elasticity (rapid elasticity)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
What should you install on your computer to support a new VR headset for VR gaming?	A capable dedicated/discrete GPU that meets the headset's VR requirements	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which best describes a Type I hypervisor?	It runs directly on the host's physical hardware (bare-metal), managing virtual machines without an underlying host OS	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud computing concept replaces a customer's local applications/programs with cloud-based resources?	SaaS (Software as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud computing concept replaces the hardware/software needed to create and test new applications from a customer's environment?	PaaS (Platform as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud concept focuses on replacing physical hardware at a customer's location with cloud-based resources?	IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud concept lets users store files in the cloud when local device space is low, and retrieve them once space is available again?	Cloud (online) storage / cloud file sync with local storage offloading	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud deployment model is dedicated to a single organization for enhanced security and control?	Private cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud deployment/pricing model uses a pay-as-you-go structure for IT services?	Public cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud model allows both onsite systems and cloud services to work together seamlessly?	Hybrid cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud model only allows your company's own employees to use the service, keeping it most secure from outsiders?	Private cloud	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud service characteristic lets you get more storage/resources added as fast as possible?	Rapid elasticity / on-demand self-service	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud service model is best suited for using pre-built applications without managing infrastructure?	SaaS (Software as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which cloud service type provides instant, quickly-provisioned access to servers and switches managed over the internet?	IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which option would you use to configure PXE for remote OS imaging during a deployment?	Enable/select PXE (network) boot in the BIOS/UEFI boot order settings	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which scenario would MOST benefit from application virtualization?	Running a legacy or incompatible app by streaming it in an isolated environment, without installing it natively on the current OS	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which type of Virtual Desktop reduces capital expenditures, with hardware maintained by the cloud provider?	Hosted/cloud-based VDI (DaaS — Desktop as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Which type of cloud service provides an end-to-end application solution for a recurring monthly or yearly fee?	SaaS (Software as a Service)	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
Why is a VM in sandbox mode ideal for testing a new application safely?	It isolates the test environment from the host OS/data, so crashes, bugs, or malware in the app can't affect the physical machine	CompTIA_A+::Virtualization_Cloud
100 Windows 10 PCs need to be locked so no one can change the boot order or boot an unauthorized OS. What feature should be enabled?	A BIOS/UEFI supervisor (administrator) password to lock boot order settings	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A MacBook can't print to the office's network printer, while Windows workstations print fine. What should be done to resolve John's issue?	Install the correct macOS-compatible printer driver (or use AirPrint if supported)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A PC shows "No bootable device found" with multiple hard drives, a DVD in the optical drive, and a USB drive plugged in. What would MOST likely resolve this?	Remove the non-bootable USB/DVD media and/or correct the BIOS/UEFI boot order to boot from the correct hard drive	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A PC won't power on; power cables are secure and the PSU (set to 110V) tests OK. What is the NEXT troubleshooting step?	Test/replace the front-panel power button and its motherboard connector, or swap in a known-good PSU to isolate the fault	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A RAID 5 drive is reporting S.M.A.R.T. errors but the array still shows no degradation. What should the administrator do FIRST?	Back up the data immediately and proactively schedule replacement of the flagged drive before it fails	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A RAID 5 file server alerts "RAID is degraded... Physical Disk 3 has failed." What is the BEST fix?	Replace the failed physical disk and allow the array to rebuild using parity	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A RAID 5 workstation is slower than normal, though diagnostics pass; clicking noises are heard from the array. What is the MOST likely cause?	A drive within the array is beginning to fail (the clicking) and degrading performance — identify and replace it	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A Roku connected via HDMI shows "Unauthorized content." What should be done to fix this?	Use an HDMI cable/port that supports HDCP (or enable HDCP on the TV/source)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A USB printer was working earlier but now fails to print, with no changes reported. What should you check NEXT?	Check the print spooler/queue for a stuck or paused print job (restart the Print Spooler service if needed)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A VoIP phone's Cat6a patch cable has been repeatedly rolled over by a chair and looks flattened. What is the most likely cause of the connectivity issue?	The cable's internal wiring/twisted pairs were physically damaged by being crushed — replace the cable	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A Windows workstation crashes with certain applications, showing a BSOD. What is the most likely cause?	A faulty or incompatible device driver, or failing RAM	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A classroom projector displays bright, correctly-sized artifacts obscuring parts of the image. What should you do FIRST?	Check/reseat the video cable connection (loose or damaged cable is the most common cause of on-screen artifacts)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A classroom projector's image is dim but clear and correctly positioned. What is the FIRST thing to do to brighten it?	Adjust the projector's brightness setting/mode (check for eco-mode) before considering a bulb replacement	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A client's computer keeps rebooting itself without warning. What is the BEST action to investigate?	Check the Windows Event Viewer logs for error details around the reboot times (and check for overheating/power issues)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A color laser printer prints small vector graphics fine but fails 60-70% through large bitmap photos (400-800 MB). What is MOST likely the reason?	The printer doesn't have enough onboard memory (RAM) to fully process such large raster/bitmap jobs	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A computer has a noisy whining sound and no dust is visible on the fans. What should you try next?	Replace (or lubricate) the failing fan — the whine is typically a worn fan bearing	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A computer keeps booting to the incorrect hard drive. What should you do?	Change the boot order/boot device priority in BIOS/UEFI to select the correct drive	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A computer keeps losing track of time and date. What is MOST likely the cause?	The CMOS battery is dying and needs replacement	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A computer won't boot, makes no sound, and smells of burning plastic. Which tool should you use to diagnose it?	A multimeter (to test the power supply's output) — after a visual inspection for obvious damage	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A customer smells a foul (non-burning) odor from inside their PC. What would you expect to find?	A leaking/bloated capacitor, or biological contamination (mold, dead insect/rodent) inside the case	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A customer's VGA cable has a few broken pins. What would MOST likely happen if they used it to connect their monitor?	Depending on which pins are broken, they may lose specific colors, see a distorted/garbled image, or get no display at all	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A customer's system clock keeps resetting, causing date/time discrepancies. What component should be investigated?	The CMOS battery (likely dying)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A domain controller takes a long time to boot and makes steady clicking noises from the hard drive. What is the BEST action to speed up boot time?	Replace the failing hard drive (ideally with an SSD)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A drawing tablet stylus feels scratchy and occasionally fails to register strokes, requiring harder presses. What is MOST likely the cause?	A worn stylus nib/tip (replace it) or a dirty tablet surface	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A grinding noise is traced to the power supply's fan, not the hard drive. What is the BEST fix?	Replace the power supply (the fan bearing is failing)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A home theater projector keeps turning off a few minutes after a new bulb was installed. What are the MOST likely causes? (Select TWO)	Overheating (dirty filter/blocked vents) and an improperly seated or incompatible replacement bulb	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop display is extremely dim even at max brightness, but the image is visible when a flashlight is pointed at the screen. What component should be replaced?	The backlight (or its inverter)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop doesn't appear to charge when plugged into a hotel room outlet. What should be tried FIRST?	Try a different electrical outlet (and verify the power adapter/cable) before assuming a hardware fault	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop has a foul odor coming from it. What is MOST likely the cause?	A swollen, leaking, or damaged battery	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop keyboard displays "he3p" instead of "help" and "n6ne" instead of "none." What is the MOST likely cause?	Num Lock is enabled, causing the embedded numeric keypad to override certain letter keys	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop monitor shows black bars on the left/right with a squashed, distorted image. What is MOST likely the cause?	The display resolution/aspect ratio is set incorrectly — reset it to the display's native resolution	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop shuts down every time it's moved, even after the HDD, RAM, LCD ribbon cable, and battery were reseated. What is MOST likely causing this?	A loose or failing internal power connector (DC jack) or battery connector on the motherboard	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop shuts down intermittently, faster during processor-intensive tasks, with no unusual odors. What is MOST likely the cause?	Overheating (thermal shutdown) — check cooling/vents/fans and thermal paste	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop with an i7 CPU, 16 GB RAM, and a 500 GB 5400 RPM HDD boots and loads programs slowly. What upgrade would BEST improve performance?	Replace the HDD with an SSD	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop works fine at its desk but powers off when moved to the conference room. What is MOST likely the cause?	It's running on a failing/depleted battery in the conference room (no power adapter connected there)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop's built-in webcam is enabled in BIOS but not detected by the OS. What is the NEXT troubleshooting step?	Update or reinstall the webcam driver	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop's motherboard has failed and won't power on, but the user needs spreadsheets stored on it. What should you do?	Remove the internal hard drive and connect it to another computer via a USB enclosure/adapter to retrieve the files	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop's screen image is displayed upside down. What is the BEST fix?	Change the display orientation setting in Windows (Display Settings), or check for an accidental orientation hotkey (Ctrl+Alt+Arrow)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop's touchscreen flickers between too bright and too dim only when plugged in at a coffee shop outlet, not at the hotel. What is the MOST likely cause?	The coffee shop outlet is supplying unstable/dirty power (poor grounding or voltage fluctuation) affecting the laptop	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laptop's wired connection isn't working, and the NIC light is steady instead of blinking. What is MOST likely the issue?	A physical link exists but no data is being passed — check the cable/switch port configuration or a duplex mismatch	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A large laser printer's output has begun showing a double/ghost image. Which component is most likely at fault?	The imaging drum (worn or not being properly cleaned/erased between cycles)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laser printer makes a crinkling sound and prints images at an angle. What should the technician do to fix this?	Check/clean or replace the paper feed and fuser rollers, and verify the paper tray guides are properly aligned	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A laser printer's output has a white streak running across the page. What should be done to fix this?	Clean or replace the imaging drum (or check for an obstruction/low toner causing the streak)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A loopback plug test shows the Ethernet port is sending packets but not receiving them. What does this indicate, and what's next?	A receive-side hardware fault (bad receive pins/transceiver) — replace/repair the NIC or port	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A macOS workstation keeps crashing with certain apps, showing a spinning rainbow pinwheel. What is the most likely cause?	Insufficient system resources (RAM) or a hung/unresponsive process/application causing the system to become unresponsive	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A multifunction laser printer still shows a paper jam error after the jammed paper was manually pulled out. What should you try FIRST?	Open all the printer's covers/trays and check for leftover torn paper fragments still stuck in the paper path	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A network printer's pages have begun showing a dust-like coating when handled. Which component should be replaced?	The fuser assembly (failing to properly bond/melt the toner)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A network-enabled multi-function printer connected via CAT5e has issues every time there's a power outage. What should you do to resolve this?	Connect the printer to a UPS (battery backup with surge protection)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A new build POSTs successfully (fans spin, LEDs light, POST completes) but shows "bootable device not found." What did the technician likely forget to connect?	The SATA data cable between the hard drive and the motherboard	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A new build's fans don't spin, the hard drive doesn't spin, and the motherboard's LEDs remain unlit. What did the technician likely forget to connect?	The power supply's main 24-pin motherboard power connector (or the PSU itself isn't switched on/plugged in)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A new build's fans spin and LEDs light, but POST never completes and the monitor stays blank. What did the technician likely forget to connect?	The CPU power connector (4/8-pin EPS12V) to the motherboard, or the RAM isn't fully seated	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A new color laser printer (only ~50 pages printed) prints the logo's blue incorrectly compared to the screen. What is MOST likely the problem?	The printer needs color calibration	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A new wireless printer is configured on the guest Wi-Fi network; drivers are installed, but a test page won't print. What is the likely cause?	The guest network isolates client devices from each other/the main LAN, so the workstation can't reach the printer — connect the printer to the main network instead	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A newly installed hard drive isn't recognized in BIOS/UEFI, though cables are verified correctly connected. What should BEST solve this?	Check BIOS/UEFI settings to ensure the SATA port/drive is enabled, and try a different SATA port/cable or update firmware	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A newly installed home theater projector shows odd debris on the screen. What should you do to correct this?	Clean the projector's lens (dust/debris is on the lens or inside the optical path, not the actual screen)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A print job on cardstock smears, but the same job on regular paper doesn't smear. What should you do NEXT?	Adjust the printer's paper-type setting for heavier stock (increases fuser heat/dwell time to properly bond toner)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A print job produces no output and no errors appear in the taskbar's printer icon. What should you try FIRST?	Check whether the printer is set offline, or restart the Print Spooler service	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A print job to the Sales printer produces nothing, but the same job prints fine on the Customer Service printer. What should you check FIRST?	Whether the Sales printer is offline, paused, or has a stuck print queue	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A printer worked during setup (test page printed), but later a user gets "access denied" when printing, even after restarts. What MOST likely caused this?	The user's print permissions on the printer were changed or removed — check the printer's security/sharing permissions	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A projector goes blank after 24 minutes, works again after a break, then fails after 4 more minutes. What is MOST likely wrong?	The projector is overheating and shutting down for thermal protection (clogged vents/failing fan, or a failing lamp)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A projector's image is trapezoidal (72" wide at top, 66" at bottom) even though resolution settings are correct. What setting should be adjusted?	Keystone correction	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A replacement laptop screen arrived with no instructions and no manufacturer manual is available. What is the BEST course of action?	Look up a third-party repair guide/video (e.g., iFixit) for that model	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A second OS was installed; "Operating System Not Found" appears even though boot.ini looks correct. What is MOST likely the cause?	The boot configuration data (BCD)/bootloader is corrupted or misconfigured for the new OS (boot.ini only applies to legacy BIOS boot, not UEFI)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A shared network printer accessed via a print server stops printing after the first of three documents. What is your FIRST step?	Restart the Print Spooler service on the print server (and clear the stuck queue)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A shared printer failed with a 2-week wait for replacement; a manager's USB printer could serve 12 employees, no wired jacks are free, but a wireless AP exists. What's the BEST solution?	Connect the PC with the shared USB printer to the wireless network (or use a wireless print server) so others can print to it over Wi-Fi	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A slow workstation shows a S.M.A.R.T. error during boot-up. What should you do FIRST?	Back up the data immediately	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A video editor's workstation makes loud clicking noises loading apps/editing video; fans were already replaced but the noise persists. What should you do NEXT?	Back up the data and replace the failing hard drive	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation has multiple S.M.A.R.T. errors, a loud clicking noise on boot, and the OS fails to load. What is MOST likely the problem?	The hard drive is failing mechanically (the "click of death") — replace it	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation in a closed wooden cabinet reboots intermittently with no pattern, though memory and cables are fine. What is MOST likely the cause?	Overheating due to poor ventilation inside the enclosed cabinet	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation loads a PXE-based OS instead of booting into Windows on reboot. What should you do next?	Check and correct the BIOS/UEFI boot order — the system is set to boot from the network (PXE) before the local drive	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation loses accurate time overnight whenever it's powered off, requiring a manual reset each morning. What is MOST likely causing this?	The CMOS battery is dying	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation runs briefly then shuts down unexpectedly; the cooling fans can be heard humming. What is MOST likely the issue?	Overheating — check CPU fan/heatsink seating, thermal paste, and dust buildup restricting airflow	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation shows "bootable device cannot be found"; UEFI doesn't recognize the hard drive, but cables are fine. What is MOST likely the issue?	The drive's SATA mode (AHCI/RAID) setting in UEFI is misconfigured, or the drive itself has failed	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
A workstation won't boot and displays "OS not found." What is the MOST likely fix?	Check/correct the boot order in BIOS/UEFI and verify the bootable drive is properly connected	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After Windows Updates installed successfully overnight, the network connection shows "limited." What rollback action should be performed?	Uninstall the recently installed Windows/driver update to restore network connectivity	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After a laptop lost power unexpectedly, it's stuck at 800x600 and the normal 1920x1080 option is missing from Display Settings. What is the cause?	The video/graphics driver was corrupted or reverted to a generic driver and needs to be reinstalled/updated	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After a reboot, the desktop background shows only a few hundred unique colors. Which setting should be reconfigured?	The display's color depth/quality (bit depth) setting	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After cloning a display to a second monitor, the second monitor's text appears twice as large. What should you configure?	Match the display resolution/DPI scaling settings for both monitors	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After installing a high-end PCIe x16 graphics card, the computer makes odd noises and shows "no source" on the monitor. What is MOST likely the issue?	The GPU's power connector isn't properly attached, or the PSU doesn't provide enough wattage for the card	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After moving from France to the US and plugging in via a power adapter, the computer's screen stays blank and the fans don't spin. What is MOST likely the problem?	The power supply's voltage selector switch is set for the wrong region's voltage (e.g., 230V instead of 120V), or a non-auto-switching adapter is being used incorrectly	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After replacing a CPU, the system boots but shuts itself down after about a minute. What step was MOST likely forgotten?	Applying thermal paste and/or connecting the CPU fan/heatsink power connector — the system is overheating and shutting down for protection	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After replacing a failed 5400 RPM drive with a 7200 RPM drive in a RAID 5 array, the array remains degraded. What is the most likely cause?	The array rebuild was never initiated — the replacement drive must be added to the array and a rebuild started via the RAID controller	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After testing with minimal components, a computer's fans spin but there is no display and no POST beep codes. What is MOST likely the cause?	The motherboard (or CPU) has failed	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
After turning off 65" plasma TVs, the company logo remains faintly visible in the upper-left corner. What should you do?	This is image burn-in/retention from static content displayed too long; vary displayed content or use a screensaver going forward to prevent further burn-in (it's typically not fully reversible)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
An 11-month-old laser printer with no maintenance and ~3,000 pages printed is fading. What is MOST likely the cause?	The toner cartridge is low and needs replacement (or a maintenance kit is overdue)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
An external monitor's screen intermittently flashes and goes black for a second before reappearing. What is the most likely cause?	A loose or faulty video cable connection — reseat or replace the cable	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
An impact printer is creasing paper, risking jams. What might be causing this? (Choose TWO)	An incorrectly adjusted platen gap and misaligned paper feed/tractor guides	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
An impact printer's output goes from darker to lighter as the print head moves left to right. What is the MOST likely cause?	The ribbon is worn or unevenly inked — replace the ribbon	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
An inkjet printer prints images/text at an angle, and sometimes not at all. What should a technician perform to align it?	Run the printer's head alignment/calibration utility	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
How can you determine if TPM is enabled on a system?	Check the BIOS/UEFI settings, or run the TPM Management console (tpm.msc) in Windows	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
How can you share a directly-connected USB printer with a coworker at no additional cost?	Enable printer sharing in Windows on the host computer so the coworker can print to it over the network	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Laser-printed pages are fading, with black more faded than the other colors. What is the BEST solution?	Replace the black toner cartridge (it's low)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Parts of a laptop's picture remain on screen even after a full shutdown/reboot, despite updated drivers and recalibration. What is MOST likely the problem?	The LCD panel itself has image burn-in/persistence — it needs to be replaced	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Susan sees streaks of toner across her printed pages. What is the MOST likely solution?	Replace the toner cartridge (a damaged/dirty drum or cleaning blade is leaving toner streaks)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
What feature should be enabled to prevent unauthorized/unsigned applications and bootloaders from loading during bootup on 100 new PCs?	Secure Boot (UEFI)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
What should you configure after installing an SSD in a laptop to increase its lifespan?	Enable TRIM support	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which symptoms would lead a technician to conclude a power supply needs replacement?	Random shutdowns/reboots, the system not powering on at all, a burning smell from the PSU, or fans failing to spin	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which symptoms would lead a technician to suspect a laptop's memory is the issue?	Random reboots, BSODs, freezing, or errors that occur especially under memory-intensive use, or memory-related POST beep codes	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which symptoms would lead a technician to suspect a workstation's RAM is the problem?	Random reboots, BSODs/system freezes, or errors that occur especially under memory-intensive tasks	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which symptoms would lead a technician to suspect the CMOS battery needs replacement?	The system clock/date resets, BIOS settings don't persist across reboots, or a "CMOS checksum error" appears at boot	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which symptoms would lead a technician to suspect the motherboard needs replacement?	Burning smell, failure to POST, bulging/leaking capacitors, or intermittent random shutdowns/lockups	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Which tool should you use to confirm the motherboard is receiving the proper amount of power?	A multimeter (or a dedicated power supply tester)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
While installing the 72nd of 150 new desktops, you smell a chemical (non-burning) odor. What component should you inspect and likely replace?	A leaking/failed capacitor on the motherboard or power supply	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
Windows 10 icons appear very large and the image is blurry. What is the most LIKELY cause?	The display resolution/scaling is set incorrectly (not the native resolution) — reset to the monitor's native resolution, or update the video driver	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
You hear a loud, rhythmic sound during a computer's operation. Which storage component is likely failing?	A mechanical hard disk drive (a failing bearing/motor)	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
You need to share one printer across a 4-computer workgroup with no switch ports or server available. What's the BEST method?	Enable printer sharing on the PC the printer is connected to, so the other 3 computers print through it over the existing network	CompTIA_A+::Hardware_Troubleshooting
